  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Retailers pay for steady sales, accurate stock and happy customers. They judge you by shift reliability, stock accuracy and how you lead a team.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is keeping a simple, accurate stock record and checking it on a fixed day.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and retail management: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools forecast demand, plan displays and answer customer queries. Routine planning and ordering shrink.
  </p>
  <p>
    Leadership, customer care and local judgment hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to plan and check; later, own the store and the team.
  </p>

